.TH SPINCLASS-SWEATFILE 5 "" "spinclass" "Spinclass Reference"
.SH NAME
spinclass-sweatfile \- sweatfile configuration format
.SH DESCRIPTION
Spinclass sessions are configured via TOML files called
.IR sweatfiles .
These control git excludes, Claude Code permissions, direnv setup,
session entrypoints, lifecycle hooks, MCP server registration, and
custom start-* plugins.
.PP
Sweatfiles are loaded as a hierarchy that merges
.I global
.RI ( ~/.config/spinclass/sweatfile )
\(-> intermediate parent directories \(-> repository-level
.RI ( <repo>/sweatfile )
\(-> worktree-level
.RI ( <worktree>/sweatfile ).
Later definitions override earlier ones according to per-field merge
semantics described below.
.PP
Intermediate parent directories are walked along
.B two
chains: the lexical ancestors of the working directory, and the
ancestors of its symlink-resolved (\fIrealpath\fR) form. Both chains
are inspected in root-first order, bounded above by
.B $HOME
(exclusive \(em loaded as the global file) when the chain runs through
home, or by the filesystem root
.RB ( / ,
exclusive) otherwise. Candidate directories are deduplicated by
canonical (symlink-resolved) path: if a directory in one chain
resolves to the same canonical path as one already loaded, the second
entry is recorded with a skip reason and not re-merged.
.PP
A given physical worktree therefore produces the same merged
configuration whether entered through a canonical path or through a
symlink, provided sweatfiles exist along both chains. When a
filesystem-only-reachable directory has a sweatfile that no path-only
chain can reach (e.g.\& entering through the canonical path skips a
sweatfile that would only be visible via a symlinked alias), the
.B sc validate
output makes this asymmetry explicit by listing every directory it
considered alongside the load/skip status.
.SH TABLES
.SS [claude]
Controls Claude Code session behaviour.
.TP
.B allow
Array of Claude Code permission rules (e.g.\&
.BR Read ", " Edit ", " "Bash(git *)" ", " "mcp__server__tool" ).
.B Merge:
nil = inherit, empty array = clear, non-empty = append.
.SS [git]
.TP
.B excludes
Array of patterns appended to
.IR .git/info/exclude .
.B Merge:
nil = inherit, empty = clear, non-empty = append.
.SS [direnv]
.TP
.B envrc
Array of direnv directive lines written to
.IR .envrc .
When nil, defaults to
.B source_up
(plus
.B use flake
if a
.I flake.nix
exists).
.B Merge:
nil = inherit, empty = clear, non-empty = replace.
.TP
.B dotenv
Table of key-value pairs written to
.IR .spinclass.env .
Values support
.B $VAR
expansion; the special variable
.B $WORKTREE
expands to the worktree path.
.B Merge:
map merge (child keys override parent keys).
.SS [hooks]
Lifecycle hooks executed as shell scripts.
.PP
The
.BR create ", " pre-merge ", " on-attach ", and " on-detach
hooks are invoked via
.B sh \-c
with the working directory set to the worktree path.
The environment variable
.B WORKTREE
is set to the absolute worktree path.
The
.B stop
hook follows a different invocation path (run by Claude Code's
.B Stop
event handler with cwd set to the session's working directory) and does
not export
.BR WORKTREE .
.TP
.B create
Script run after worktree creation (before session attach).
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B stop
Script run when the Claude Code session ends (via Stop hook).
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B pre-merge
Shell script run by
.B sc merge
after the worktree branch has been rebased onto the default branch but
before the fast-forward merge into it.
If the script exits non-zero, the merge is aborted and the worktree is
left in its rebased state so the user can fix the issue and retry.
Typical use: run tests or linters as a pre-merge gate.
When this hook is set, the spinclass PreToolUse hook auto-approves the
.B mcp__plugin_spinclass_spinclass__merge-this-session
and
.B mcp__plugin_spinclass_spinclass__check-this-session
tools (whichever is registered \(em see
.B disable-merge
below) so Claude Code does not prompt: the pre-merge hook acts as the
gate instead.
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B pre-merge-output-format
String. One of
.BR raw " (default) or " tap-ndjson .
Controls how spinclass interprets the
.B pre-merge
hook's stdout when assembling the
.BR merge-this-session " / " check-this-session
response. When set to
.BR tap-ndjson ,
spinclass parses the hook's stdout as a TAP-14 ndjson stream via
.B tap/go/pkgs/{reader,ndjson}
and, on failure, emits each failing test record as a structured
.B failure:
field in the YAMLish diagnostic instead of the trailing-N-lines
.BR tail: .
The madder blob referenced by
.B resource_link:
holds the parsed ndjson rather than the raw stdout, and the MCP
.B ResourceLinkContent
block's
.B mimeType
is set to
.B application/x-ndjson
(versus
.B text/plain
when
.BR format = raw ).
On parse failure (the hook didn't actually emit TAP, or emitted zero
parseable records), the response falls back to a 15-line
.B tail:
of raw stdout so degenerate output is still visible.
The
.B tail:
field remains the default visibility signal when
.BR format = raw .
.B sc validate
rejects any value outside the closed set
.BR { raw,\ tap-ndjson } .
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B on-attach
Script run when a session attaches to the worktree, fired by
.B sc start
or
.B sc resume
after the session state file has been written but before the
configured session entrypoint
.RI ( "[session].start " "or " "[session].resume" )
is exec'd.
Typical use: warm caches, kick off background helpers (e.g.\& a tmux
side-pane, a watcher process), or emit a session-start log line.
A failing
.B on-attach
script is logged as a warning but never blocks session start \(em it
must not gate attach.
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B on-detach
Script run when the session detaches from the worktree, fired by
.B sc start
or
.B sc resume
after the entrypoint exits and the session state has been updated
to
.BR running-detached " or " inactive
(per the
.B [session].liveness-probe
result).
Typical use: tear down on-attach side processes, post a session-end
notification, or rotate logs.
A failing
.B on-detach
script is logged as a warning; spinclass continues with cleanup
either way.
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B disallow-main-worktree
Boolean.
When true,
.B sc resume
refuses to attach to the main worktree.
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B tool-use-log
Boolean.
When true, a PostToolUse hook logs tool invocations.
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B disable-merge
Boolean.
When true,
.B sc merge
exits non-zero before any git operation runs, and the
.B merge-this-session
MCP tool is replaced in the tool catalog by
.B check-this-session
\(em the two tools are mutually exclusive, gated on this flag.
.B check-this-session
runs the configured
.B [hooks].pre-merge
command without merging, providing an agent-CI surface for repositories
where merges must go through external review (e.g., protected branches
that require pull requests). The
.B sc check
CLI subcommand is available regardless of this flag.
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B disable-nix-gc
Boolean.
When true,
.B sc close
and
.B sc clean
skip the post-removal worktree-scoped Nix garbage collection.
By default (or when this flag is unset), spinclass enumerates the gc
roots whose link path resolves into the worktree being removed,
expands each root's closure, and attempts
.B nix-store \-\-delete
on each path; nix's own liveness check refuses paths still kept alive
by other roots, so the blast radius is bounded to "what only this
worktree was holding."
The
.B sc close \-\-nix\-gc=<true|false>
flag overrides this setting per-invocation.
The collection is a silent no-op when
.B nix-store
is not on
.BR PATH ,
or when the worktree has no gc roots.
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.SS [session\-entry]
Controls what command is exec'd when attaching to a session, what
environment is injected, how liveness is detected after detach, and how
long tombstones are retained.
.TP
.B start
Argv array for new sessions.
Defaults to
.BR $SHELL .
Each element supports
.B $VAR
expansion against the session environment, so
.B \[dq]$SPINCLASS_SESSION_ID\[dq]
substitutes at exec time.
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B resume
Argv array for resumed sessions.
When nil, falls back to
.BR start .
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B liveness\-probe
Argv array exec'd after the entrypoint returns, to distinguish
.BR running\-detached
from
.BR inactive .
Exit 0 means the session is still attachable in the multiplexer;
non-zero (or 2-second timeout) means it's gone.
Inherits the session env including any keys from
.BR [session\-entry].env .
Typical zmx-style probe:
.B "[\(dqsh\(dq, \(dq-c\(dq,\ \(dqzmx -g \\\(dq$SPINCLASS_GROUP\\\(dq list --short | grep -qxF \\\(dq$SPINCLASS_SESSION_ID\\\(dq\(dq]" .
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.TP
.B tombstone\-retention
Duration string (e.g.
.BR 30d ,
.BR 0
to keep forever) controlling how long
.B sc clean
preserves tombstone entries before reaping.
.B Merge:
scalar override.
.SS [session\-entry.env]
Subtable map of environment variables injected into every session
process (entrypoint, hooks, liveness probe).
Keys are strings, values are strings.
This is a generic env-injection mechanism with one convention:
.B SPINCLASS_GROUP
is the customary key for a multiplexer-group name so the
.B liveness\-probe
argv can reference it symbolically instead of hardcoding the group in
two places.
Spinclass-owned variables —
.BR SPINCLASS_SESSION_ID ,
.BR SPINCLASS_REPO ,
.BR SPINCLASS_BRANCH ,
.BR SPINCLASS_WORKTREE ,
.BR SPINCLASS_DESCRIPTION ,
.BR TMPDIR ,
.BR CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR
— are applied AFTER this map and so cannot be clobbered.
.B Merge:
per-key map merge (child wins on collision, parent-only keys survive).
.SS [[start\-commands]]
Array of tables declaring custom
.BI sc\ start\- name
subcommands.
See
.BR spinclass\-start\-commands (7)
for the full schema and JSON protocols.
.B Merge:
dedup-by-name (later definition replaces earlier one in-place).
.SS allowed\-mcps
Top-level array of MCP server names to auto-approve in
.IR .claude/settings.local.json .
These servers must be registered externally (e.g.\& in the user's
.IR ~/.claude.json ).
.B Merge:
nil = inherit, empty = clear, non-empty = append.
.SS [[mcps]]
Array of tables declaring MCP servers to register in
.I .mcp.json
and auto-approve.
.TP
.B name
(required) Server name.
Used as the key in
.I .mcp.json
and in
.IR enabledMcpjsonServers .
.TP
.B command
Executable to run.
A name-only entry (empty command) acts as a removal sentinel,
removing an inherited server.
.TP
.B args
Argv passed to
.BR command .
.TP
.B env
Table of environment variables set on the server process.
.TP
.B auto-allow
Array of strings forming an argv vector
.RI ( "command arg1 arg2 \&..." ).
The first element is the executable; remaining elements are its arguments.
When present, spinclass execs this command at session start to
discover tool-level permissions.
See
.BR "AUTO-ALLOW PROTOCOL" .
.PP
.B Merge:
dedup-by-name (full entry replacement, same as
.BR [[start\-commands]] ).
Every entry with a non-empty
.B command
implicitly adds to the allow-list.
.SS [[pre\-merge\-skills]]
Array of tables declaring skill names that the agent must address
before
.B merge\-this\-session
or
.B check\-this\-session
will run the pre-merge hook.
When the resolved list is non-empty, those MCP tools refuse to proceed
until a fresh attestation has been recorded via the companion
.B nothing\-but\-the\-truth
tool, which spinclass registers automatically alongside whichever of
.BR merge\-this\-session " / " check\-this\-session
is active.
The terminal CLI
.RB ( "sc merge" ", " "sc check" )
is unaffected.
.TP
.B name
(required) Skill identifier as it appears in the Claude Code skill
catalog (e.g.\&
.BR eng:code-reviewer ", " simplify ", " security-review ).
A name-only entry (empty or absent
.BR rationale )
acts as a removal sentinel, removing an inherited skill from the
resolved list.
.TP
.B rationale
Free-form string describing why the skill is required for this repo
or sweatfile scope.
The text is echoed back to the agent in the gate-failure response and
must be addressed in the agent's per-skill reasoning.
.PP
.B Merge:
dedup-by-name (full entry replacement, same as
.BR [[mcps]] ).
A non-empty resolved list activates the attestation gate; an empty
or absent list leaves merge behaviour unchanged.
.PP
See
.B PRE-MERGE SKILL ATTESTATION
below for the
.B nothing\-but\-the\-truth
tool's input schema, lifecycle, and gate-failure response shape.
.SH AUTO-ALLOW PROTOCOL
The
.B auto-allow
field on a
.B [[mcps]]
entry declares a command that spinclass executes at session creation
time.
The field is a TOML array of strings forming an argv vector: the first
element is the executable, and any remaining elements are arguments
passed to it.
The command must print a single JSON object to stdout describing which
of its tools should be added to
.B permissions.allow
in
.IR .claude/settings.local.json .
.SS Execution Context
The auto-allow command runs after
.I .mcp.json
is written but before the session entrypoint is exec'd.
The working directory is the worktree root.
The command inherits the session's environment, including any variables
set via the
.B [env]
table in the sweatfile hierarchy.
The command is exec'd directly (not via a shell); wrap in
.B sh \-c
if shell features are needed.
.SS JSON Schema
.RS 4
.nf
{
  "tools": ["tool_name_1", "tool_name_2"]
}
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B tools
(required) Array of bare tool names.
Names must
.B not
include the
.B mcp__
prefix; spinclass constructs the fully-qualified form
.BI mcp__ name __ tool
using the server's
.B name
field.
.SS Error Handling
.IP \(bu 2
If the command exits non-zero, the error is reported to stderr and the
session is still created.
.IP \(bu 2
If stdout is not valid JSON or does not match the schema, a warning is
printed to stderr.
.IP \(bu 2
If any tool name contains the
.B mcp__
prefix, it is rejected.
.IP \(bu 2
If the response contains a
.B servers
field, it is rejected.
MCP servers cannot auto-allow other servers.
.SS Examples
.B Basic: MCP server with built-in auto-allow subcommand
.PP
The server itself exposes an
.B auto-allow
subcommand that lists its safe-to-auto-approve tools:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[[mcps]]
name = "moxy"
command = "moxy"
args = ["serve"]
auto-allow = ["moxy", "auto-allow"]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Running
.B moxy auto-allow
might produce:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
{
  "tools": [
    "lsp_execute-command",
    "grit_commit",
    "grit_diff",
    "rg_search"
  ]
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
Spinclass constructs fully-qualified permission rules and adds them to
.BR permissions.allow :
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mcp__moxy__lsp_execute-command
mcp__moxy__grit_commit
mcp__moxy__grit_diff
mcp__moxy__rg_search
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Shell wrapper: dynamic tool list from an external source
.PP
When the auto-allow logic requires shell features (pipes, subshells),
wrap the command in
.BR "sh \-c" :
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[[mcps]]
name = "db-tools"
command = "db-mcp"
args = ["serve"]
auto-allow = ["sh", "-c", "db-mcp list-tools --safe | jq '{tools: .}'"]
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Minimal: allow all tools from a small server
.PP
For a server with few tools that are all safe to auto-approve, the
auto-allow command can return a static list:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
[[mcps]]
name = "formatter"
command = "fmt-mcp"
args = ["serve"]
auto-allow = ["sh", "-c", "echo '{\"tools\": [\"format\", \"check\"]}'"]
.fi
.RE
.SH PRE-MERGE SKILL ATTESTATION
When a sweatfile's resolved
.B [[pre\-merge\-skills]]
list is non-empty, spinclass registers an additional MCP tool,
.BR nothing\-but\-the\-truth ,
and gates
.BR merge\-this\-session " / " check\-this\-session
behind it.
.SS Gate behaviour
On invocation, if no fresh attestation is buffered in the session
state file
.RI ( ~/.local/state/spinclass/sessions/<hash>-state.json ),
the gated tool fails before running any pre-merge hook with a
TAP-14 response containing
.B required_skills
(the full list, each entry's
.B name
and
.BR rationale )
and
.BR required_tool: \ nothing-but-the-truth .
.PP
Each merge attempt consumes one attestation. After consumption the
record is cleared; a subsequent merge requires a new attestation
call against the current diff. There is no sticky once-per-session
mode.
.PP
The terminal CLI
.RB ( "sc merge" ", " "sc check" )
bypasses the gate entirely.
.SS nothing-but-the-truth input schema
.RS 4
.nf
{
  "skills": [
    {
      "name":      "eng:code-reviewer",
      "used":      true,
      "reasoning": "Ran the review; addressed one nil-check finding."
    },
    {
      "name":      "simplify",
      "used":      false,
      "reasoning": "Single-line bugfix, no abstraction surface to prune."
    }
  ]
}
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B skills
(required) Array containing exactly one entry per skill listed in
the resolved
.BR [[pre\-merge\-skills]] .
Names must match exactly; missing or unrecognised names fail
validation.
.TP
.B skills[].name
(required) Skill identifier matching a
.B [[pre\-merge\-skills]]
entry.
.TP
.B skills[].used
(required) Boolean.
True if the skill was invoked for this diff; false otherwise.
.TP
.B skills[].reasoning
(required) Non-empty free-form string. The tool does not police
length, style, or content \(em the act of writing the reasoning
down is the deliverable.
.SS Validation
Validation is strict on presence (every listed skill must have an
entry, names must match exactly, reasoning must be non-empty) and
lenient on content. On failure the tool emits a TAP error listing
missing and unrecognised names so the agent can correct and retry
without re-fetching the skill list.
.SS Mutual exclusivity with [hooks].disable-merge
The companion tool tracks the active gated tool:
.IP \(bu 2
.B disable-merge
unset/false plus a non-empty
.B [[pre\-merge\-skills]]
list registers
.B merge\-this\-session
and
.BR nothing\-but\-the\-truth .
.IP \(bu 2
.B disable-merge = true
plus a non-empty
.B [[pre\-merge\-skills]]
list registers
.B check\-this\-session
and
.BR nothing\-but\-the\-truth .
.IP \(bu 2
An empty or absent
.B [[pre\-merge\-skills]]
list leaves
.B nothing\-but\-the\-truth
unregistered.
.SH MERGE SEMANTICS
Each field uses one of these merge strategies when combining files in
the hierarchy:
.TP
.B "nil = inherit, empty = clear, non-empty = append"
Used by array fields:
.BR claude.allow ", " git.excludes ", " direnv.envrc ", " allowed-mcps .
A nil value (key absent) inherits the parent's value.
An explicitly empty array clears inherited values.
A non-empty array is appended to the parent's list.
.TP
.B "scalar override"
Used by single-value fields:
.BR hooks.create ", " hooks.stop ", " session-entry.start ", etc."
The child's value replaces the parent's entirely.
.TP
.B "dedup-by-name"
Used by array-of-tables:
.BR [[start-commands]] ", " [[mcps]] ", " [[pre-merge-skills]] .
Entries are matched by
.BR name ;
a later entry replaces the entire earlier entry in-place (not a
field-level merge).
New names are appended.
.TP
.B "map merge"
Used by
.BR direnv.dotenv " and " mcps.env .
Child keys override parent keys; parent keys not present in the child
are preserved.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/spinclass/sweatfile
Global sweatfile (lowest precedence).
.TP
.I <parent-dir>/sweatfile
Intermediate parent directory sweatfiles.
.TP
.I <repo>/sweatfile
Repository-level sweatfile.
.TP
.I <worktree>/sweatfile
Worktree-level sweatfile (highest precedence).
.TP
.I .claude/settings.local.json
Generated by spinclass from sweatfile config.
Contains
.BR permissions.allow " and " enabledMcpjsonServers .
The
.B spinclass
MCP server itself and its Claude Code hooks
.RB ( PreToolUse ", " Stop ", " PostToolUse )
are loaded once per session via the clown plugin manifest shipped at
.IR <plugin-share>/hooks/hooks.json ,
not mirrored into this file.
.TP
.I .mcp.json
Generated by spinclass when at least one user-declared
.B [[mcps]]
entry is present.
Contains MCP server registrations from those entries; the
.B spinclass
MCP server is loaded via the clown plugin and is not written here.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spinclass (1),
.BR spinclass\-start\-commands (7),
.BR spinclass\-validate (1)
